  "worked_solution": "Let's start by recalling the graph of $y={5}^{x}:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14194531/assets/31c990964a5a04c4a44773bb00d1b097999951b823e3b10861d13e38c364b8b5.png)\n\nNow, let's look at each statement:\n\n- Statement I is false, since the range of $f(x)={5}^{x}$ is $(0,\\infty ).$\n\n- Statement II is true, since for $x<0$, the graph gets close to zero as we decrease $x.$\n\n- Statement III is true.\n\nIn conclusion, only statements II and III are true.",
